te`:** it returned `(year, day, month)`. It now returns `(year, month, day)`.\n2. **`ledger/report.py`, `top_items`:** it sorted by total ascending, so it returned the smallest items first. It now sorts by total descending, with ties broken by item name ascending, as the docstring says.\n3. **`ledger/money.py`, `format_cents`:** negative amounts came out wrong. For example, `-310` formatted as `-$-4.90` instead of `-$3.10`, because floor division and modulo were applied to the negative number. It now splits the absolute value with `divmod` and adds the sign separately.\n\nI tried to check a few more `parse_amount` and `format_cents` edge cases (`-0.05`, `.5`, `5.`, `-100000`), but that command wasn't approved, so I didn't run them. Reading the code, `parse_amount` handles those inputs correctly. It doesn't handle a sign written after the dollar sign (`$-3.10`), but the docstring only documents `-$3.10`, so I left it alone.","ttft_ms":2195,"type":"result","duration_ms":18444,"uuid":"8fe3471e-f493-4b07-8c48-93fab2b11764","ttft_stream_ms":949,"time_to_request_ms":25,"first_content_frame_ms":949,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
